# MOONWITNESS XV — Architecture, Brand, Content & UI Integration Reconciliation

**DRAFT FOR OWNER REVIEW — NOT COMMITTED.**
**Audit date:** 2026-10-26 (Asia/Jakarta)
**Repository:** https://github.com/bjo163/moonwitnessxv
**Latest rechecked HEAD:** `7e8483e5973279572d6777532d15afc494a83f36` (`main`); initial audit baseline `4c6344625597d5fb479967db07d3b52a0ddc6147`.
**Evidence method:** connected GitHub source/tree/document/CI inspection; current SHA `7e8483e` has **successful CI run 40296311027** (including frozen install and monorepo verification). No running browser screenshots, local unpublished changes, or production deployment inspected. Revalidate HEAD and CI before execution.

## 1. Final decision and purpose

**No additional apps** are approved by this draft. Keep six existing applications: `apps/dock`, `apps/headquarters`, `apps/cockpit`, `apps/radio` (accepted future name `apps/arsy` under M28), `apps/aigateway`, `apps/sentinel`. Treat `packages/moonui` as the shared component/design runtime; Moonframe remains an external candidate design/behavior foundation, not a confirmed installed 15-skin runtime. No second API/ORM/identity/publishing authority.

- Dock is the **public experience**: Discover, Read, Explore, Research publications, Witness publications, Stories, Signal, optional World and Journey. Public data must pass release/rights gates.
- Headquarters is the **human-operated workspace**: Source stewardship, research review, SHADOW story/editorial, publishing, 100CENTER tasks, radio admin, system administration.
- Cockpit / Moondeck is the **local developer/operator supervisor**: processes, ports, logs, builds, preview, diagnostics, optional player. It must not approve research/publish or become an unprotected remote service.
- ARSY is the **single MoonQL Fastify/API/data authority**, physically `apps/radio` until M28 compatibility migration. Radio remains D09 SIGNAL, not a removed feature.
- AI Gateway is a **bounded internal inference service**, not public research authority. It must not silently send sensitive data to fallback providers.
- Sentinel is a **bounded internal collection worker** with explicit credentials and egress policy. Not a self-authorizing reviewer.

## 2. Evidence-status vocabulary (non-interchangeable)

Use distinct, typed concepts:

1. `implementationMaturity`: `planned | prototype | implemented | verified` (code/test maturity).
2. `availability`: `disabled | unavailable | degraded | available` (deployment health/capability).
3. `contentReview`: `draft | submitted | reviewed | disputed | rejected | retracted` (M14 research review; don't imply publication).
4. `publication`: `unreleased | eligible | released | withdrawn` (M18, *not* automatically inferred from research approval).
5. `sourceRights`: scoped to exact work/expression/edition/asset/license/version; unknown is denied for protected bytes.
6. `origin`: `historical-primary | editorial-adaptation | demonstrator | source-verified | modeled | AI-candidate`.

Never present simulated metrics, seeded candidates, static conceptual system lists or unlabeled generated results as live operations. Explicitly include checked timestamp, version, owner, and evidence where required.

