## 4. Product experience vs visual grammar

**Product journeys** (what users do) are not **visual modes/skins** (how interfaces render). Public journeys: Discover, Read, Explore, Research, Witness, Stories, Signal, World, Journey. HQ workspaces: Mission Control, Sources, Research Desk, Lexicon/Ontology, SHADOW, Publishing, 100CENTER, Radio Ops, System. Cockpit sections: Services, Logs, Build, Port/Environment, Preview, Diagnostics; Media is optional.

MoonUI owns component semantics, accessibility, design-token roles and shared implementation. Apps own page composition and route-specific content. Moonframe 15 skins/30 appearances are a future tested adapter capability, not currently functional in XV. A consumer brand overlay must not alter focus/keyboard/status semantics or globally rewrite Moonframe skins. Reader requires high legibility and source-centric hierarchy; creative pages may apply experimental manga/zine graphics; Cockpit is a dense operational console.

### Route-resolution principles

- One root Next layout per Dock route: remove nested `SiteLayout` from `/reader/compare`, `/prisms`, `/timeline`, `/studio` (verified in source). Preserve one header/footer/main.
- Existing `/stations`, `/reader`, `/terms`, `/figures`, `/constellation`, `/research`, `/missions`, `/patches`, `/denpa`, `/schedule` and other URLs remain supported. New `/explore`, `/research`, `/stories`, `/signals` are optional human-navigation aliases/landing routes, not replacement tables or breaking endpoint renames.
- `/studio` in Dock means **Vector Studio**, not HQ **MoonQL Data Studio** and not the future SHADOW editorial studio.
- Prefer four/five discoverable top-level nav groups instead of 14 equal priority header links; ensure pathname-based `aria-current`, keyboard/mobile menu, correct CTA targets.

## 5. Brand and narrative constitution

MOONWITNESS is the end-user brand. EMPIRE OF THE LIGHT is umbrella context; A-L-L-A-H is a technical acronym. ALLAH is a religious referent, not an application/agent or claim of software authority. ARSY = technical Hub; al-‘Arsh as scripture referent remains distinct. SHADOW editorial workspace != Shadow story character. ZILL tasawuf lens != ZILL Shadow Witness; `ZIIL` remains source-specific spelling/alias. THE BATTERIES is a fictional creative character, not a divine identity. MIZAN is an evidence evaluation method, not eschatological judgment. G.O.D.99 fictional roles != Asmaul Husna 99 != 99 editorial chapters != 99 human states. The 33 World Patches are documented proposals/reports/conflicts; never imply divine approval or authorize high-consequence action.

**Found contradiction:** `docs/decisions/M06-03-ii-lore-recovery.md` lists the II eight-era names `Origin & Genesis`, `Ancient Alliances`, ... `The Witness Horizon`, while `apps/dock/src/app/timeline/page.tsx` hardcodes `BEFORE LIGHT`, `THE ARRIVAL`, ... `NEXT PHASE` and implies heritage provenance. Represent versions as distinct `historical-primary` and `editorial-adaptation`, with exact original source SHA, not one falsely authoritative era list. `docs/decisions/M02-01-disambiguation-registry.md` describes G.O.D.99 as a code for 99 chapters whereas the Master Vision separates fictional slots from chapter count; reconcile via a source-aware ADR erratum.

