## 7. New-app decision test (hard gate)

A new `apps/*` is disallowed unless ALL these evidence items exist: (1) different security boundary or release/deployment lifecycle, (2) inability to meet it via modular workspace/worker, (3) explicit canonical data owner and API contract, (4) budget/security/operations maintenance plan, (5) a superseding ADR, (6) user decision. No new app for Prisms, 100CENTER, SHADOW, UNILEX, World Monitor, Comic/Poster tools, History, Journey or radio.

## 8. Cross-repo integration constraints

- Moonframe is separate and experimental for XV; use cross-repo SHA-pinned compatibility proof only. Do not copy skins, assets or branded marks blindly.
- All other past MoonWitness/Empire/Rocksoul repositories are **historical/source references**, not a competing current implementation authority; reviewed imports must be lineage- and rights-aware.
- Source owner, stable ID, exact edition, license and hash are distinct. Derived search/graph caches can be rebuilt; they are not alternate sources of truth.
- One generated typed SDK may read models/views and explicit endpoints, but clients must not widen ACL just to make a UI work.
- One workflow ledger; 100CENTER and SHADOW UIs do not create independent approval engines or identities.

## 9. Exact integration acceptance matrix

| Gate | Evidence required |
|---|---|
| G0 CI | Node 24/pnpm lock, clean checkout/frozen install, verify including SDK, tests, web build; publish exact SHA and CI URL |
| G1 Security | Cockpit/API origins+auth/CSRF, AI provider scope/egress, Sentinel credentials, deny-by-default model ACL and guest tests |
| G2 Rights | no unknown-rights source text on public compare, release/withdraw invalidates projections, human approval on exact revision |
| G3 Domain | ID + domain owner matrix, no duplicate model/table, metadata/source lineage and adapter registration |
| G4 Narrative | distinguish primary II vs creative adaptation eras, 99 counts, fiction/religious referents, claims vs satire, rights citations |
| G5 Frontend | single SiteLayout, route intent, nav mobile, 4 presentation modes vs 9 journeys, no fake status, one shared MoonUI behavior |
| G6 A11Y/Visual | 360/390/768/1024/1440px, light/dark when supported, RTL Arabic/Hebrew, focus/keyboard/contrast/reduced-motion, screenshots+behavior |
| G7 Release | Radio tests, Docker/PG + restore, HQ approval/nonapproval, absent AI behavior, source/consent gates, human go/no-go |

## 10. Safe execution while another local AI is working

1. `main` is the approved forward branch, but no force-push, branch generation, reset, destructive cleanup or unsupervised overwrite. Preserve uncommitted local work; coordinate a **single writer** to central files and releases.
2. Before every packet: fetch latest `main`, compare with this pinned SHA, inspect changed paths and overlapping owner. If a different agent modified the same module, **re-audit/rebase plan**, do not replay a stale patch blindly.
3. One durable task-status owner remains `TODO.md` (203 parent IDs), not this draft, a second TODO, or a set of duplicate GitHub issues. The previously proposed `UIX-001..070` are *audit child labels* only; map them to existing Mxx-yy parent IDs. Every task must have one accountable owner; secondary dependencies listed separately.
4. Mark `existing code` distinct from `DoD verified`. Completion needs source SHA, test commands+results, policy/rights evidence, reviewer where required, new SHA and CI status. When blocked, record BLOCKED/UNKNOWN.
5. Prioritize blocked security and provenance work over cosmetic UI/skin exploration. Local assistant should use small non-overlapping file scopes and serial coordination for package manifests, lockfile, generated SDK, root routes and documentation index.
6. This RFC is a draft prepared outside GitHub. No commit/push/issue/edit has been performed in this audit.

## 11. Proposed sequence (not an additional milestone system)

**Phase A / Stop-the-bleeding** — CI already green at `7e8483e` (recheck on next HEAD); address Cockpit authorization, AI Gateway egress, Sentinel credentials, Journey privacy, public Research candidate exposure, Compare rights; preserve tests.
**Phase B / Semantic contract** — one owner per domain, versioned source/fiction taxonomy, status capability contract, rewrite inaccurate name mappings via ADR errata.
**Phase C / Product separation** — Dock IA + shell fix; HQ operational truth/reviewer; Cockpit canonical UI, single local process supervisor.
**Phase D / Design consolidation** — MoonUI semantic roles + WCAG + RTL, Moonframe adapter spike (do not claim 15 skins shipped).
**Phase E / Real full-stack journey** — one exact QS 2:82 Reader→Term→Figure→Research reviewer→rights decision→approved public version; Radio unbroken; side routes remain optional.
**Phase F / Release evidence** — M27, human review, SHA-pinned screenshots & behavior, PG and Docker, restore, rollback, changelog, canary/hold decision.

**DO NOT COMMIT** before explicit follow-up approval for implementation. This text is a candidate for updating existing XV documents once compared with a *new* HEAD, not a superseding ADR now.
